"""Tests for scripts/live-verify-fi-loop.py.

Stage 2a: framework, ``pre`` part, placeholder parts.

Covers:
  G1  --stage prod → exit 1 before any AWS call (guard: stage refused before client)
  G2  allowed op through guard reaches dead endpoint (EndpointConnectionError, not GuardViolation)
  G3  write op in pre guard raises GuardViolation (read-only part)
  G4  per-part allowlist: pre allows reads, raises on writes
  X1  exit 0 when all pass
  X2  exit 1 when any FAIL
  X3  exit 2 when any SKIP (no FAIL)
  C1  check() passes on_fail to FAIL rows; detail on PASS rows
  P1  placeholder parts SKIP "not built yet" with no AWS call
  P2  all placeholder parts are distinct from pre
  S1  signal SIGINT installs → SystemExit(143) from __main__ guard
  S2  _defer_signals_for_restore holds SIGINT/SIGHUP during critical section
  S3  subprocess with PYTHONPATH stripped: SIGINT → rc 143 via runpy.run_path
  I1  subprocess import test: lazy imports all load from temp cwd
  W1  pre drive (pass): all preconditions satisfied → all PASS, manifest written
  W2  pre precondition fail: Tier 2 Lambda code readers.py has rcr.name → FAIL
  W3  pre precondition fail: Tier 2 Lambda code select_recalls.sql missing join → FAIL
  W4  pre precondition fail: recall_campaigns_issued Glue table missing → FAIL
  W5  pre precondition fail: received view SQL has no recall_campaigns_issued → FAIL
  W6  pre precondition fail: ESM is Disabled → FAIL
  W7  pre precondition fail: DLQ non-empty → FAIL
  W8  pre precondition fail: corpus has no component_name → FAIL
  W9  pre precondition fail: open LIVETEST record exists → FAIL
  W10 pre manifest written at 0600 on success

Run:
    PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest scripts/tests/test_live_verify_fi_loop.py -v
"""
from __future__ import annotations

